[00000]-*** error ***
[00001]-You are standing in a small clearing in the forest, There is a large stone cliff to the immediate east. Paths lead off to the north, west, and south.
[00002]-You are in a large open field, to the north you can see a large forest. A rushing sound can be heard from the west.
[00003]-You are standing at the top of a natural cliff overlooking a huge rushing river. A nice sandy beach is clearly visible at the base of the cliffs, far below.
[00004]-You are standing on a sandy beach beside a very large river. A large set of rapids causes the water to roar tremendously.
[00005]-You are walking through the forest, vision in any direction is blocked by the trees, except for the bright blue sky which is clearly visible above.
[00006]-In this clearing is a large old dead tree stump.
[00007]-The forest gets thicker here, you seem to be walking endlessly.
[00008]-You are in thick forest, deep scratch marks in the ground suggest that something has been dragged through here recently.
[00009]-You are standing in a small clearing in the forest, debris is strewn about the ground as if this were some kind of garbage dump. A solid steel grate is fixed into the ground here.
[00010]-You are in a small rectangular room, dimly lit by a large dome-shaped rock, glowing in the ceiling with an erie green light. A small dark passage leads north. A very narrow crack in the western wall might allow you to pass.
[00011]-You are in what appears to be a huge dining room, dimly lit by the flickering light of blazing brazisers hanging from brackets on the ornate walls, high above your head. A long and sturdy dining table is set with places for six. The chairs are cushioned with the finest velvet. A massive open door leading south is the only exit.
[00012]-This appears to be the kings study. A huge roaring fireplace in the east wall is lighting the room with an eerie flickering light. The shadows seem to dance upon the walls as if alive with some evil presence. A hugh oak desk and chair are standing in the center of the room. The walls are decorated with various paintings and ornaments. Exits in the north, south, and west walls are plainly visible as they are through huge ornate arches, which reach from floor to ceiling.
