[00015]-You are in a rough stone cavern, beneath a 3x3 steel grate. The floor is quite damp, and seems to give a little as you walk. A wide brick corrider leads away to the north, while low narrow passages lead to the east, south and west.
[00016]-You are in a large underground room, three huge pillars support the ceiling high above your head. The room is quite dusty, it seems it has not been used in a very long time. A passage exits to the west. A small sign on the wall bears the inscription "farley".
[00017]-This is an intersection of passages, which lead off to the north, east and west.
[00018]-You are in a small room, the only exit is a small passage to the east. The floor is quite damp here, and actually has small pools of water on it. Visible in the walls are the claw marks of some huge animal. <gulp!>
[00019]-You are walking along the passage which suddenly turns at a ninty degree angle, with exits to the west and south.
[00020]-This is a tee intersection, with good passages entering from the north and west, and a small narrow passage leading south.
[00021]-You are in a small dead-end cavern, the only exit leads to the north.
[00022]-Here the passage opens up into a large room, with exits to the east and west. an old lamp holder is attached to the wall here, but the lamp is long gone. There is much debris strewn about the floor.
[00023]-This room has exits to the north and east. A large shiny brass sign on the western wall reads "None who enters shall ever leave".
[00024]-The remains of a human skeleton can be seen in a small alcove in the passage, although many of the bones appear to have been crushed.
[00025]-This is a large natural underground cavern. A small stream enters from the northwest, and exits to the southeast. Small shadows can be seen darting back and forth within the stream. Good pasages exit to the east and south, and a tight corrider leads north.
[00026]-This is the entrance to what appears to be some kind of religious worship area. A large statue of a fish-headed manlike creature is visible in the north end of the room. A wide brick corrider leads south.
[00027]-You are standing in the north end of a large underground room, which seems to be some kind of gathering area. Filling the north end of the room is a huge statue of a man with a fish's head. Its eyes seem to follow you as you move about the room. Small stone benches occupy the remainder of the rooms floor space. Behind the statue you can see a tiny little stone door.
[00028]-The passage takes a sharp turn here, exiting to the east, and through a little stone door to the south.
[00029]-You are in a small circular room, which seems to be a dead end. The walls are very damp, and ooze drops of water as you watch. A small rotted desk here is cluttered with papers and other debris.
[00030]-This is a small 10 by 10 chamber, made from loose fitting brick. A small passage leads west through a little door, and a rickity looking ladder disappears through a hole in the floor.
[00031]-You are in a small secret chamber, which is much drier that the other rooms you have been in. A narrow passage exits to the south.
[00032]-You are in a small circular chamber, with rough walls. A ladder leads up through a hole in the ceiling, and small passasge exits to the north.
[00033]-This is a small square room, obvious passages exit to the north, south, and west. A large rock in the center of the room bears the inscription "Beyond this point - there be dragons".
[00034]-This is a huge underground cavern, with a sparkling stream which rushes into a roaring whirlpool, disappearing through the floor. A narrow catwalk allows you to walk around the spectacle. Good passages exit to the north, and south, and narrow crawl leads east. A few wisps of white mist are floating lazily near the ceiling.
[00035]-You have entered a tiny north/east corner. A cloud of white mist is emerging from the northern exit.
[00036]-The passage ends here in a flat rock face, except for a narrow slit continuing to the east. White steamy mist is billowing from the slit. The main passage leads off to the south.
[00037]-You are in a large dome shaped room, above a lake of molten lava. A stream entering from the ceiling and falling into the lava lake is instantly vaporized, the steam clouds make it nearly impossible to see. The heat is unbearable, I don't think you should stay here very long. A narrow rickity stairway leads down.....
[00038]-This is the boneyard, the floor is knee deep in bones of animal and human origion. A good passage exits to the south, and a tight narrow crawlway leads east.
