[00088]-You are standing in a small cavern with a three foot hole in the ceiling from which a long rope is hanging. A passage leads south into darkness. The west side of the cave ends in a giant fissure, which is so deep you can't see the bottom.
[00089]-This is a three corner juction, with passages going north, south, and east. The walls are slightly warm towards the southern passage.
[00090]-You are in a small brick room with no obvious exits except for a passage leading west. The southern wall of the room is slightly warmer than the other walls.
[00091]-You are in a north/south passage which is very warm, the passage to the south is even warmer, and from it a roaring sound can be heard. A small crawlway leads off to the east.
[00092]-This room is so hot you have trouble breathing. A single passage exits to the west. The southern wall is too hot to touch.
[00093]-A north/south passage ends here, and a tight narrow passage leads east. A loud roaring sound can be heard from the eastern passage. It is very hot, causing it to be very uncomfortable. The heat seems to be billowing out of the eastern passage.
[00094]-You are at the edge of a breath-takeing view. For below you is an active volcano, from which great gouts of molten lava come surging out, cascadeing back down into the depths. The glowing rock fills the farthest reaches of the cavern with a blood-red glare, giving everything an eerie macabre appearance. The air is filled with flickering sparks of ash and a heavy smell of brimstone. The walls are very hot to the touch, and the thundering of the volcano drowns out all other sound. Embedded in the jagged roof far overhead are myriad twisted formations composed of pure white alabaster, which scatter the murkey light into sinister apparitions upon the walls. To one side is a deep gorge, filled with a bizarre chaos of tortured rock which seems to have been crafted by the devil himself. Am immense river of fire crashing out from the depth of the volcano, burns its way through the gorge, and plummets into a bottomless pit far of to your left. To the right, an immense geyser of blistering steam erupts continuously from a barren island in the center of the sulfurous lake, which bubbles ominously. The far right wall is aflame with an incandescence of its own, which lends an additional infernal spelendor to the already hellish scene. A dark foreboding passage exits to the west.
[00095]-You are on the west side of the fissure, a good passage exits to the south, and a small crawl leads west.
[00096]-You are in a small anteroom off the main passage. The floor, walls, and ceiling are like polished glass. A crawlway leads east from here.
[00097]-You are standing on the north side of an immense crevice. A white mist billowing from the distant bottom of the crevice obscures view of the other side. A narrow dangerous-looking rope bridge leads south accross the chasm.
[00098]-You are standing on the south side of the crevice. The white mist is thich here, seeming like ground fog. Passages exit to the south, and to the west. A narrow dangerous-looking rope bridge leads north accross the chasm.
[00099]-You are in a damp sideroom of the misty chasm, filled with oddly shaped limestone formations. A solitary passage exits to the east. A solid looking trapdoor is fixed into the floor of the cavern here.
[00100]-You are in a tiny dead end chamber. A small stream enters and exits through small slits in the east and west walls. The only exit is to the north.
[00101]-This is a little dead end, with a passage leading east. Rough stone steps cut into the wall lead up to a trapdoor in the ceiling.
[00102]-You are is a small circular chamber with gravel covering most of the floor. Etched into the east wall is the outline of a large skull and crossbones. Good passages exit to the north and south, and a narrow crawlway veers off to the west.
[00103]-You are at a tee intersection between a north passage and an east/west passage. The eastern passage is very narrow, and seems to wind and twist.
[00104]-You are at a dead end of a long winding passage leading west. There is an extremely narrow crack in the eastern wall of the passage. A really small adventurer might be able to get through.
[00105]-You are in a small square chamber, with many cobwebs on the ceiling. The dust on the floor must be at least two inches thick. There are no tracks in the dust, its obvious that no-one has been here for many centuries. There is a large sign on the northern wall, which reads:      "Congratulations on bringing light into the dark room".  A small dimly lit passage leads south.
[00106]-The passage takes a sharp turn here, and continues to the east and to the south. Small fossil shapes are visible in the walls.
[00107]-You are at a junction of three passages, exiting to the north, west, and south.
[00108]-This is the "soft" room. Thick curtins cover the walls . A thick carpet of moss covers the floor and ceiling. It is very quiet here. Passages exit to the east and west.
[00109]-You are at a tee intersection between a north/south passage, and a tight passage leading east. The ceiling is very low here.
[00110]-You are in a large flat room, with passages exiting to the north, south, east, and west. Hanging from the ceiling is a huge iron frame containing many sharp spikes. It looks dangerous.
[00111]-This is a small narrow passage leading east/west. Deep groves in the floor lead out of a northern passage, suggesting that something heavy has been dragged through here.
[00112]-You are a point where a narrow southern passage meets a long east/west passage. recent chisel marks in the wall would seem to indicate that the passage has been expanded recently.
[00113]-A long wide passage from the west gets narrow here, and makes a sharp turn, continuing to the north.
[00114]-The main passage turns here, exiting to the west, and south, and a small four foot high crawlway splits off, and leads east.
[00115]-The walls of this room are covered with many pre-historic cave paintings. Scenes of great hunts, and bloody wars are depicted. Predominant among the paintings is a huge scene showing a mighty dragon breathing fire, and burning a small band of cavemen. This scene is so large, it takes up the entire eastern wall. A narrow four foot high crawlway exits to the west.
[00116]-You are standing in a small round room, with exits to the east and south. A heavy wooden sign in the northern end of the room displays the message "WELCOME ADVENTURER" in solid bold looking letters.
[00117]-You are in a small secret room, carved out of solid rock. A solitary exit leads south.
[00118]-Marks on the wall here indicate much recent activity. A large wooden sign anchored to the rock floor bears the message:    "TURN BACK - AREA OFF LIMITS - CAVE UNDER CONSTRUCTION"   "   BEYOND THIS POINT --- WITT CONSTRUCTION COMPANY   "  The main passage from the south ends here, but a small newly cut passage continues to the north.
[00119]-You are at WITTS END, passages lead off in *ALL* directions.
[00120]-You are walking along a small ledge circling a deep cavern. The bottom of the cavern is shrouded by mist, and cannot be seen. Strange splashing sounds can be heard echoing up from the depths. The ledge ends in a northern and eastward passage.
[00121]-You are standing in a small twisted room, at the top of a flight of rickity wooden stairs. The only other exit is to the south.
[00122]-You are at the west end of a wide brick hallway, at the foot of a set of rickity wooden stairs. This looks like some kind of  buried castle. The hallway leading east is made entirely of bricks which appear to be in remarkably good condition (Considering the circumstances). A small stone side passage leads south.
[00123]-You are in the middle of a long east/west hallway made of brick. The ceiling in this hallway is quite low, you almost have to stoop to walk in it. A solid iron door is fixed into the south wall.
[00124]-This room looks like an unused art studio. Most of the pictures have been defaced by other adventurers over the years. Various bits of broken artists equipment is strewn about the floor. The only exit is a small hallway to the north.
[00125]-Here a wide brick hallway leading west joins up with a huge north/south hallway with walls of finely crafted wood inlays. The ceiling of this hallway must be at least 20 feet high.
[00126]-You are at the north end of a huge hallway, with walls of finely crafted wood inlays. A faint flicker of light is visible through a massive open door to the north, and a small passage exits to the west.
[00127]-You are walking along a narrow stone corrider running east/west. A small room is visible through a small archway in the north wall.
[00128]-This room is obviously the bedroom of the castle owner. A large four poster bed is predominent in the north end of the room. A huge bureau style dresser is located along the east wall, and a large closet in the west wall appears to be empty. Exit is through an arch in the south wall.
[00129]-You are in a huge ballroom. The ceiling, high above your head is formed of majestic looking arches. From the exact center of the ceiling hangs a beautiful crystal chandelier. The walls are made of oak and walnut panels, with finely crafted mahogany inlays. Hallways exit to the north, west, and to the south. The ballroom floor is made of smooth marble tiles.
[00130]-This appears to be an outside entrance to the castle. To the south a huge open underground cavern is visible, and a wide hallway leads north.
[00131]-This is the main entry hall to the castle. Directly to the south is a huge open underground cavern. A wide hallway leads north, and a narrow passage leads west. There is a small door in the east wall.
[00132]-This look like a small side entrance to the castle. To the south, a huge open underground cave is visible. A wide hallway leads north.
[00133]-You are standing in a huge open underground cave. Directly in front of you is a huge pit, from which strange splashing sounds can be heard. The cavern continues upward, but the ceiling is shrouded in mist, and is not visible. The main entry door to a huge underground castle is visible to the north, paths east and west lead to smaller side doors of the castle. The air in this cavern is remarkably fresh. A small winding trail leads south, around the pit, and out into the cavern.
[00134]-The trail ends here, at the edge of a huge cavern. Barely visible to the north is the outline of a large castle. A small three-foot hole leads down from here, into darkness....
[00135]-You are in a small cloakroom, off from the main castle entrance. There are many racks for hanging coats etc. here, but most of them are empty. A small door in the west wall is the only exit.
[00136]-You are standing in a small natural cavern, with carved steps leading up to a three foot hole in the ceiling. A narrow low passage exits to the north.
[00137]-Here a narrow passage from the south widens to meet with a wide brick corridor from the north. The north passage can be seen to end at a large door which seems to be a the lower castle entrance.
[00138]-You are standing just inside what is obviously a lower level entrance to the castle. The walls are made of huge bricks, and the ceiling appears to be a wall of mud, which looks like it might fall at any minute. Good passages exit to the east and west, and a wide brick corridor leads away to the south. The squeaking of mice can be heard from within the walls.
[00139]-This is the south-east corner guardroom of the castle, deserted except for the mice which can be seen scurrying about the floor. Slits for archers to shoot through are positioned at regular intervals around the walls of the circular room, although they are plugged with mud now. Exits are to the north and west.
[00140]-This is a long hallway, running north/south through the castle. The walls are lined with candle holders, which are now empty. The dusty floor shows no tracks save for a mirad of mice footprints. A small narrow side hall veers of to the west.
[00141]-This small room appears to have been taken over by the mice. The floor is littered with excrement, the stench is overpowering. In one corner is a huge pile of rubbish, from which mice can be seen comeing and going. Every so often a mouse glares at you with little red eyes.
[00142]-This is the north-east corner guardroom, deserted except for the occasional mouse which scurrys past, disappearing through the doorway in the south wall. There is another doorway in the  west wall.
[00143]-This is a long east/west hall, plain in every detail, except for a small door in the north wall, above which is a a sign reading:       "VENDING MACHINE STOREROOM - KEEP OUT"
[00144]-This is the south-west corner guardroom of the castle. It appears to be quite clean, and free of dust. Faceing large slits in the west and south walls are huge cannon mountings, although the cannons are gone. There are open doorways in the north and east walls.
[00145]-This is a huge trophy room. The walls of the room are painted with brilliant scenes of battle. The head of some huge beast is hanging on display from the west wall, far above your head. A small passage exits to the east, and larger passages exit to the north and south.
[00146]-This looks like is used to be the castle workshop. An assortment of broken and worn out tools litter the floor around a sturdy workbench which is standing against the eastern wall. The rest of the floor is covered with wood shaveings and other bits of debris. The only exit is through a tiny little passage in the middle of the western wall.
[00147]-This looks like the north-west corner guardroom of the castle. The walls are very damp, and you can see mud oozing in through the arrow slits in the walls. Water is also dripping from the ceiling which is bulging so that the middle hangs very low. Exits are to the east and south.
[00148]-You are in a small square room with a door in the south wall. The floor is littered with scraps of paper and cloth. The east and west walls are lined with sturdy cabinets which have all been broken open and are empty. A set of sturdy shelves line the north wall.
[00149]-This is a small secret 10 foot circular room, with a small passage exiting to the south. A three foot hole in the exact center of the room leads down. A small rope ladder is firmly fastened to the floor nearby, and leads down the hole.
[00150]-You are is a little 10 x 10 chamber, with a rope ladder leading up through a hole in the ceiling. A small tunnel leads south.
[00151]-You are in the middle of a curved hallway, beside a small tunnel in the north wall. The walls and floor are made of a sturdy grey brick. The hallway continues to the east and west.
[00152]-This is the north end of the castle dungeon. A wide hallway exits from the north end of the room, which continues to the south. To the immediate east is a small cell, with solid looking iron bars covering the doorway.
[00153]-You are standing in the middle of the dungeon room. The room extends to north and south. About the room are various instruments of torture, and a row of stocks along the west wall still contain some of the bones of those who were imprisoned there. In the center of the room is a huge firepit, above which are hanging several empty sets of shackels. To the east is a small cell, behind solid looking iron bars.
[00154]-This is the south end of the castle dungeon, a narrow passage exits from the south wall of the room, which extends to the north. There is a small cell in the east wall, behind solid looking iron bars.
[00155]-This 5 x 5 cell is barren and empty.
[00156]-In this cell you find the bones of its last occupant, lying in a heap near the back wall, among scraps of tattered rags.
[00157]-This cell is nearly empty, except for a line of ants marching in a straight line accross the floor of the room. Scrawled in the dust on the south wall is the message: "Killroy was here!"
[00158]-This hallway curves here, continuing to the east and west. A dirty passage exits through the south wall.
[00159]-This looks like the guards quarters, three small beds are lined up along the east wall. Empty tables and benches have been roughly shoved against the west wall. Various bits of debris are scattered about the dirty floor. A small dirty passage exits to the north.
[00160]-This is an intersection of passages, a wide curving hallway exits to the north and south, while a narrower straight passage leads away through an arch in the west wall.
[00161]-This is the east end of the main castle hallway. An arch in the north wall leads to a small room, and a narrower passage continues to the east. From the south wall, a small passage leads away. The ceiling is so high it not visible in the darkness.
[00162]-This looks like a small storeroom. A sturdy wooden table at the far end of the room is supporting a large wooden keg, wich has a large faucet fastened to the side of it. Various other shelves and closets are empty. The only exit is through the the door, which is to the south.
[00163]-You are standing in the middle of the main castle hallway, which continues to the east and west. Dim flickering shadows can be seen through an archway in the northern wall. High above your head, you can barely discern the faint shimmer of a huge crystal chandlier. There is a small round table standing against the west wall.
[00164]-This was obviously the castle library. Giant bookcases entirly fill the north, east and west walls. The floor is cushoned with a soft carpet, and it is very quiet. Most of the books are gone now, and those that remain seem to be worthless, as they are severly damaged.
[00165]-You are in a small corner room of the castle, a huge archway leads to the east, where you can see a faint flickering of light. Another doorway leads south.
[00166]-This is the west end of the main castle hallway. An arch in the north wall leads to a small room, and a narrower passage exits to the south. A huge door in the west wall leads away to darkness....
[00167]-You are in the west end of a side passage, which travels parrallel to the main castle hall. To the north, the passage opens up and joins the main hall.
[00168]-This is a small alcove in a side passage, which bends here, procedeing to the north and west.
[00169]-You are standing just outside the main castle gates. which are to the immediate east. This is an immense cavern which seems to extend upward indefinitely, the ceiling is invisable in the darkness above the sheer rock faces of the walls. Large pools of water splashed about the cavern ripple gently in the small swirling breezes blowing through the passage. Huge gapeing exits are visible to the north, south, and west.
[00170]-You are in a fractured corridor, just off the main passage. Although this passage appears to run north/south, the north part is completely blocked by bolders. A small side passage exits to the west.
[00171]-The passage opens up into a small room here, with exits in the east and west walls. Delicate carving in the northern wall forms ancient runes, which appear to glow and dance, even as you watch.
[00172]-The passage forms a tee intersection here, with a north/south corridor meating up with a small passage from the east.
[00173]-You are is a small cramped corner, to the north, a passage leads away, and seems to open up. Another small passage leads west.
[00174]-This is a wide spon in a long east/west passage. The south wall of the passage has a huge burn mark on it, as it it were struck by fire or lightning of some kind.
[00175]-The main passage curves here, and continues to the north and east. A narrow passage through a fissure in the rock exits to the south.
[00176]-This is a small sphere shaped dead-end room. The ceiling, walls and floor are shaped into smooth curves. A strange looking ridge in the wall runs around the entire room, at a point halfway between the floor and ceiling. Along this ridge are many books, potions, powders and other trinkets, although you cannot get close to them to take a better look, because you keep slipping on the smooth slippery floor. Visible on that floor are several sets of barefoot prints, which appear to lead up to the shelf as if the person makeing them had no problem walking at all. A large circular desk is fixed in the south wall, and has a circular bench running around it, although you cannot get close to it either. It appears to be covered with numerous papers and scrolls, and a big quill pen can be seen protruding from a large ink-well sitting there. A small circular hole exits to the north.
[00177]-You are standing in an immense cavern, beside a huge underground lake. The beach extends to the west from here. To the east it ends in a sheer rock face, except for a small hole from which a passage exits. To the south you is another sheer rock face, and the lake extends beyond sight to the north.
[00178]-This cavern is by far the largest you have been in so far, It extends beyond sight in all directions except for the sheer rock face directly to the south, from which a wide passage exits. A huge underground lake to the north extends farther that you can see. The beach you are standing on continues to both the east and west.
[00179]-An underground lake ends here, beside a sheer rock face to the west, from which a small passage extends. The lake expands to the north, for farther than you can see. The beach extends to the east, and a sheer rock face presents itself to the immediate south.
